WEBVTT

00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:15.790
The first competition of the Grand Prix Series.

00:00:15.790 --> 00:00:19.080
The Ionodai members tried
to skate safely and steadily,

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:21.910
but I, the brilliant Hayato Sasugai,

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:25.450
suggested that they switch to
a performance more befitting of challengers.

00:00:25.450 --> 00:00:26.620
However, this ended in the worst result...

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:29.040
"6. Ionodai High School"

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:29.040
However, this ended in the worst result...

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:32.290
I hope it's not getting
everyone down too much...

00:00:31.870 --> 00:00:33.290
"Chutei University Kamimaezu
1st Overall in First Competition"

00:00:33.290 --> 00:00:35.370
"Chutei University Kamimaezu
1st Overall in First Competition"

00:00:33.290 --> 00:00:35.370
"At the first competition
of the Grand Prix Series,

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:38.410
"Chutei University Kamimaezu
1st Overall in First Competition"

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:38.410
Chutei University High School,
who placed sixth last year,

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:40.750
"Chutei University Kamimaezu
1st Overall in First Competition"

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:40.750
placed first with their solid performance
and high-level unison skating

00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:44.870
"Chutei University Kamimaezu
1st Overall in First Competition"

00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:44.870
in both the short program and free skate,
shining at overall first place."

00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:45.410
"Stark Contrast Between Seeded Schools"

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:48.500
"Stark Contrast Between Seeded Schools"

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:48.500
"On the other hand, for last year's
fourth place school, Ionodai High School,

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:52.370
even though they were able to get high
scores with second in the short program,

00:00:52.370 --> 00:00:54.580
their score nosedived with
their free skate performance.

00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:55.410
As a result,

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:58.700
they have a difficult start to the
competition in sixth place overall."

00:00:58.700 --> 00:00:59.950
That's what it says.

00:00:59.950 --> 00:01:01.870
Jeez, what should we do?

00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:04.370
If the same thing happens next time, we'll lose.

00:01:04.370 --> 00:01:05.750
No, it's fine.

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:06.790
Why?

00:01:06.790 --> 00:01:07.910
We still have time.

00:01:07.910 --> 00:01:09.160
Not really.

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:10.830
We're in sixth overall, you know?

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:13.750
That's like the furthest from
the finals you could be!

00:01:13.750 --> 00:01:14.620
Aki!

00:01:14.620 --> 00:01:18.040
I'm never believing what Sasugai says again.

00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:19.120
I've decided.

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:22.330
Sorry, but I feel the same way.

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:27.330
Hey.

00:01:27.330 --> 00:01:28.870
After taking into account
the results of the first competition,

00:01:28.870 --> 00:01:31.700
I've brought a few options
for how to change the routine.

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:33.910
Let's get started and...

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:39.950
Oh?

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:13.500
"Episode 7
Resolve"

00:03:16.830 --> 00:03:19.330
What's with this atmosphere?

00:03:19.330 --> 00:03:21.160
I mean, I can guess...

00:03:21.160 --> 00:03:23.080
We still have two more competitions.

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:24.160
We can still turn it around.

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:26.200
I hope so.

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:28.870
I'm going to go running.

00:03:28.870 --> 00:03:30.410
Me, too...

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:37.410
Hey, Maeshima...

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:41.910
Maeshima!

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:43.580
What the hell's wrong with him?

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:45.540
Sasugai, try to understand.

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:49.120
My stomach hurts...

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:51.370
Mine, too...

00:03:51.370 --> 00:03:53.000
Maeshima!

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:54.620
Hey!

00:03:54.620 --> 00:03:57.290
What the hell do you want? Smiling like that.

00:03:57.290 --> 00:04:00.790
With those results.
We got sixth, you know! Sixth!

00:04:00.790 --> 00:04:03.080
It's because you said that all of a sudden!

00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:05.120
We could've done better than that!

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:07.580
Even if we didn't get first,
we could've been second!

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:11.700
I wouldn't've had to show Shinozaki
that pathetic performance...

00:04:13.540 --> 00:04:15.200
Feel better?

00:04:22.040 --> 00:04:25.950
"Galaxy on Ice
An Ice Show Shining in the Galaxy"

00:04:39.620 --> 00:04:42.080
An article on the first competition?

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:43.540
Mr. Miura.

00:04:43.540 --> 00:04:45.250
It's written well, right?

00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:48.660
It's just a shorter version
of what was in the paper, though.

00:04:48.660 --> 00:04:49.870
What are you doing here?

00:04:49.870 --> 00:04:51.830
I'm babysitting the newbie.

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:54.750
It's her first job as a reporter.

00:04:54.750 --> 00:04:59.000
I was relatively free, so I was
ordered to come with her.

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:01.790
What about you? What are you doing here?

00:05:01.790 --> 00:05:04.290
Watching an ice show rehearsal?

00:05:04.290 --> 00:05:06.620
I have permission from the school, you know.

00:05:06.620 --> 00:05:10.500
To practice myself when I have time, too.

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:14.830
The reason for Ionodai
High School's loss is clear.

00:05:14.830 --> 00:05:16.830
In an about-face from his stability
during the short program,

00:05:16.830 --> 00:05:21.450
Maeshima became much livelier,
and Kiriyama and the others tried to follow.

00:05:21.450 --> 00:05:24.250
However, they couldn't catch up...

00:05:24.250 --> 00:05:26.700
Maeshima was focused on his own performance,

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:29.620
Terauchi and Kiriyama were watching Maeshima,

00:05:29.620 --> 00:05:34.580
and Jonouchi and Akimitsu
were trying to follow the two of them.

00:05:34.580 --> 00:05:37.410
They were all looking in different directions.

00:05:37.410 --> 00:05:41.450
That threw them all off, until eventually...

00:05:41.450 --> 00:05:43.620
...they broke down.

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:46.790
They were like an orchestra without a conductor.

00:05:46.790 --> 00:05:52.620
But, that ambitious,
provocative skating wasn't bad...

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:56.580
It made me feel like there was
another possible ending...

00:05:56.580 --> 00:06:01.200
I don't think I was the
only one who felt that way.

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:02.580
I wonder.

00:06:02.580 --> 00:06:04.790
Will you continue coaching them?

00:06:04.790 --> 00:06:09.540
You said something before, right?
About not wasting time or something.

00:06:09.540 --> 00:06:11.660
What do you want me to do, Mr. Miura?

00:06:11.660 --> 00:06:15.750
What? I'm the one asking <i>you</i> .

00:06:15.750 --> 00:06:20.040
If you're here at practice, it means
your back is returning to normal, right?

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:23.000
If you're going to go back
to competing, then stop coaching.

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:25.120
You'll be able to focus on practicing that way.

00:06:25.120 --> 00:06:28.620
And those boys will be able
to practice under a new coach.

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:33.450
That's what I meant by not wasting time.

00:06:33.450 --> 00:06:37.830
Don't waste their time just because
of your own circumstances.

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:43.910
They're aiming to win nationals,
and this is their only chance.

00:06:43.910 --> 00:06:47.370
Sorry, I went too far.

00:06:47.370 --> 00:06:51.160
Like I said before, I'm Takumi Adachi's fan.

00:06:51.160 --> 00:06:54.790
I'll support you no matter
what decision you make.

00:06:56.870 --> 00:06:57.080
"Keyaki Park Ice Arena"

00:06:57.080 --> 00:06:58.370
"Keyaki Park Ice Arena"

00:06:57.080 --> 00:06:58.370
Okay, see you tomorrow.

00:06:58.370 --> 00:06:59.410
"Keyaki Park Ice Arena"

00:06:58.370 --> 00:06:59.410
Good work today.

00:06:59.410 --> 00:07:00.700
"Keyaki Park Ice Arena"

00:06:59.410 --> 00:07:00.700
See ya.

00:07:19.700 --> 00:07:21.250
Good work today.

00:07:23.870 --> 00:07:26.250
Adachi, do you have a minute later?

00:07:27.790 --> 00:07:31.750
I think we should have
the coach take a look, after all.

00:07:31.750 --> 00:07:34.950
But you know, he's hands-off, or rather,

00:07:34.950 --> 00:07:37.120
he acts like he's not interested in us.

00:07:37.120 --> 00:07:41.080
But during our club match,
he taught us, didn't he?

00:07:41.080 --> 00:07:43.950
We definitely leveled up with that.

00:07:43.950 --> 00:07:46.160
If he teaches us like that again,

00:07:46.160 --> 00:07:49.910
since he's such a good skater,
I'm sure he has moves we don't know yet--

00:07:49.910 --> 00:07:51.790
Is that guy really that amazing?

00:07:51.790 --> 00:07:54.120
Huh?! You don't know?

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:58.540
Will you turn pro?

00:07:58.540 --> 00:08:00.540
Competing costs money.

00:08:00.540 --> 00:08:01.830
Even if you have sponsors,

00:08:01.830 --> 00:08:04.250
your main source of income
is that school you're coaching at, right?

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:08.370
My agency said we could
treat you exceptionally well.

00:08:08.370 --> 00:08:10.540
I'm sure you'd like what they offer.

00:08:12.790 --> 00:08:16.620
"I haven't won yet"... right?

00:08:16.620 --> 00:08:18.910
It's what you used to always say.

00:08:18.910 --> 00:08:21.040
"I haven't gotten to the top yet.

00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:25.450
If I still have the chance to,
then I don't want to give up yet."

00:08:25.450 --> 00:08:28.160
Do you still feel that way?

00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:34.410
You can tell me your answer later.

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:36.080
Take your time and think about it.

00:08:46.870 --> 00:08:49.120
You could call this the coach's special move--

00:08:49.120 --> 00:08:54.950
A quadruple Axel, quadruple toe loop,
and quadruple loop all in a row.

00:08:54.950 --> 00:08:56.910
He did it once in a competition,

00:08:56.910 --> 00:08:59.000
but no one's successfully landed it since.

00:08:59.000 --> 00:09:02.120
It's hard if you aren't blessed physically,

00:09:02.120 --> 00:09:03.580
but on top of the difficulty of the move,

00:09:03.580 --> 00:09:06.910
it's hard to incorporate into a routine.

00:09:06.910 --> 00:09:08.290
Tomo! One more time!

00:09:08.290 --> 00:09:10.620
Oh, r-right...

00:09:10.620 --> 00:09:15.250
Second at All-Japan, career-high
ranking of 8th in the world,

00:09:15.250 --> 00:09:18.870
and placing at many other top-tier competitions.

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:22.160
The media doesn't cover him as much anymore,

00:09:22.160 --> 00:09:25.370
but before he was injured,
a lot of people had their eyes on him.

00:09:25.370 --> 00:09:29.200
His brusque nature made some
people keep their distance, though...

00:09:29.200 --> 00:09:31.660
When I first met him, it was funny
how he was exactly as I'd imagined.

00:09:31.660 --> 00:09:33.870
Oh, yeah.

00:09:33.870 --> 00:09:35.410
He really is amazing.

00:09:35.410 --> 00:09:38.330
Yeah... His technical skill
and his expressiveness...

00:09:46.120 --> 00:09:48.040
Coach!

00:09:48.040 --> 00:09:49.500
What do you guys want?

00:09:49.500 --> 00:09:51.750
This place is off-limits
to the public right now.

00:09:51.750 --> 00:09:53.790
Sorry, we got permission to come in.

00:09:53.790 --> 00:09:58.000
Teach me how to do that
three-quadruple jump combination!

00:09:58.000 --> 00:09:58.950
--Idiot!
--Ouch!

00:09:58.950 --> 00:10:01.370
We came to ask you again.

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:04.000
We want to skate in the Grand Prix finals.

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:05.660
We want to get first place in the nation.

00:10:05.660 --> 00:10:08.660
Please teach us in order for us to do that!

00:10:08.660 --> 00:10:10.700
Please!

00:10:10.700 --> 00:10:12.910
What are you guys aiming for?

00:10:12.910 --> 00:10:14.700
To become pros? To compete at the world level?

00:10:14.700 --> 00:10:19.080
Do you want to win now for future prestige?

00:10:19.080 --> 00:10:20.000
That's--

00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:23.160
You said you wanted me to teach you
that three-quadruple jump combination.

00:10:23.160 --> 00:10:25.450
Yeah! I watched a video of you skating it!

00:10:25.450 --> 00:10:27.080
It was amazing! So--

00:10:27.080 --> 00:10:30.870
That was something I spent years perfecting.

00:10:30.870 --> 00:10:33.290
Asking me to teach you just like that?

00:10:33.290 --> 00:10:36.790
You don't seem to understand the value of it.

00:10:36.790 --> 00:10:39.370
Go home! You're interrupting my practice.

00:10:41.870 --> 00:10:44.330
What's wrong? Didn't you hear me?

00:10:47.330 --> 00:10:51.200
Jeez! Maeshima, it's your fault
we made the coach mad!

00:10:51.200 --> 00:10:53.580
I-It's all <i>my</i> fault?

00:10:53.580 --> 00:10:57.200
Speaking of which, I haven't seen Sasu recently.

00:10:57.200 --> 00:10:59.790
Do you think it's hard for him
to come since he messed up?

00:10:59.790 --> 00:11:03.290
He's not going to quit
the club like this, is he?

00:11:03.290 --> 00:11:05.580
That seems kind of sad.

00:11:05.580 --> 00:11:07.160
So many problems.

00:11:07.160 --> 00:11:09.580
Yeah, it's the same as usual, though.

00:11:09.580 --> 00:11:12.700
Damn it, just you wait!

00:11:19.000 --> 00:11:25.290
"13th Boys' High School Skate-Leading
Grand Prix Series"

00:11:19.000 --> 00:11:25.290
The Boys' High School Skate-Leading
Grand Prix Series has begun.

00:11:25.290 --> 00:11:28.450
"2nd Competition Results"

00:11:25.290 --> 00:11:28.450
Here are the results of the second
competition, which was held today.

00:11:28.450 --> 00:11:33.500
"1. Kogahara High School
2. Chutei University Kamimaezu High School"

00:11:28.450 --> 00:11:33.500
In second, Chutei University High School,
who got first in the first competition.

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:37.200
"1. Kogahara High School
2. Chutei University Kamimaezu High School"

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:37.200
And in first place this time, the school
that placed first in the preliminaries,

00:11:37.200 --> 00:11:40.200
"1. Kogahara High School
2. Chutei University Kamimaezu High School"

00:11:37.200 --> 00:11:40.200
Kogahara High School, in their
first appearance in this series.

00:11:40.200 --> 00:11:45.370
You skated in both the first and second
competitions. Did that lower your score?

00:11:50.200 --> 00:11:54.910
No, we were able to skate in the second
with the good image left from the first,

00:11:54.910 --> 00:11:56.750
so I think it was actually better.

00:11:56.750 --> 00:11:59.200
Anything to say about
your remaining competition?

00:12:01.250 --> 00:12:06.870
We'll do our best to keep this up
and skate without any regrets.

00:12:10.500 --> 00:12:13.450
This was your first competition
in the series. Were you nervous?

00:12:13.450 --> 00:12:15.330
No, not really.

00:12:16.410 --> 00:12:20.700
It's remarkable to be able to get
first place in your first appearance!

00:12:20.700 --> 00:12:22.250
Any thoughts about that?

00:12:22.250 --> 00:12:23.700
Not particularly.

00:12:24.910 --> 00:12:28.580
You received the highest marks
in one competition--

00:12:28.580 --> 00:12:31.120
Are you finished? I need to practice.

00:12:32.250 --> 00:12:35.250
I didn't think Himekawa's team would do so well.

00:12:35.250 --> 00:12:36.250
Yeah...

00:12:36.250 --> 00:12:40.160
Overtaking the team with the
Ishikawa brothers to get first place

00:12:40.160 --> 00:12:42.910
and also getting the highest number
of points in one competition.

00:12:42.910 --> 00:12:45.080
"1. Kogahara High School
2. Chutei University Kamimaezu High School
3. Kanazawa Nishiizumi Kogei High School"

00:12:42.910 --> 00:12:45.080
And with this point difference...

00:12:45.330 --> 00:12:46.540
To put it simply,

00:12:46.540 --> 00:12:50.750
does this mean we'd lose to Himekawa's team
even if we skated against them now?

00:12:50.750 --> 00:12:53.040
It's not that simple, though.

00:12:53.040 --> 00:12:55.540
Shouldn't we ask the coach for help, after all?

00:12:55.540 --> 00:12:58.750
Won't he just kick us out again?

00:12:58.750 --> 00:13:00.500
Where's Maeshima?

00:13:01.700 --> 00:13:03.660
Is he skipping with Sasugai?

00:13:03.660 --> 00:13:05.000
Seriously?

00:13:05.000 --> 00:13:09.290
Um, Sasugai hasn't been coming
to school recently, either...

00:13:09.290 --> 00:13:10.370
Huh?

00:13:10.370 --> 00:13:12.200
And he's not picking up the phone...

00:13:12.200 --> 00:13:14.250
What, like he's missing?

00:13:14.250 --> 00:13:16.540
Don't tell me...

00:13:16.540 --> 00:13:18.830
I don't think this is the case,

00:13:18.830 --> 00:13:21.000
but what if he was down about
what happened the other day...

00:13:21.000 --> 00:13:23.080
...and committed suicide, or something?

00:13:23.080 --> 00:13:25.200
Hey, don't say that!

00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:26.120
How long has it been?

00:13:26.120 --> 00:13:28.910
Since he stopped coming to club...

00:13:28.910 --> 00:13:30.370
This is...

00:13:30.370 --> 00:13:32.120
I didn't bully him!

00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:33.500
I didn't bully him, okay?

00:13:33.500 --> 00:13:34.660
Calm down.

00:13:34.660 --> 00:13:35.790
Do you know Sasugai's address?

00:13:35.790 --> 00:13:36.870
No, I don't.

00:13:36.870 --> 00:13:38.700
It should be in the school register.

00:13:38.700 --> 00:13:40.540
I'll go check!

00:13:40.540 --> 00:13:41.660
--It's not true, right? Say it's not true! Right?

00:13:41.660 --> 00:13:44.450
--What's Maeshima doing at a time like this?
--It's not true, right? Say it's not true! Right?

00:13:56.660 --> 00:13:57.750
A park...?

00:13:57.750 --> 00:14:01.750
Th-This is the address I got...

00:14:02.750 --> 00:14:04.950
Could it be a fake address?

00:14:04.950 --> 00:14:07.700
I wonder why he would do something like that...

00:14:07.700 --> 00:14:09.200
That guy...!

00:14:09.200 --> 00:14:10.250
Where's Maeshima?

00:14:10.250 --> 00:14:12.450
He won't answer his phone.

00:14:12.450 --> 00:14:13.410
Oh!

00:14:13.410 --> 00:14:14.370
What is it?

00:14:14.370 --> 00:14:16.830
Um, at the first competition,

00:14:16.830 --> 00:14:20.120
when I was walking with Sasugai,
we saw Shinozaki...

00:14:20.120 --> 00:14:21.950
He didn't say anything about it,

00:14:21.950 --> 00:14:24.870
but it seemed like they'd known
each other for a long time.

00:14:24.950 --> 00:14:27.450
"St. Clavis Gakuin"

00:14:27.450 --> 00:14:29.040
"St. Clavis Gakuin"

00:14:27.450 --> 00:14:29.040
Oh, what is it, Tomo?

00:14:29.040 --> 00:14:30.830
--Taiga, Taiga, Taiga, Taiga!
--You're in the middle of club, aren't you?

00:14:30.830 --> 00:14:33.830
--Yeah, but Sasugai is--right, you wouldn't know.
--Oh, yeah, that pastry--

00:14:33.830 --> 00:14:36.540
--Shinozaki, Shinozaki!
Will you give me his number?
--What, Shinozaki?

00:14:36.540 --> 00:14:39.120
Shinozaki, Taiga, Shinozaki,
Taiga, Shinozaki, Taig--

00:14:39.160 --> 00:14:40.870
"Taiga"

00:14:41.160 --> 00:14:42.330
He's calling!

00:14:47.620 --> 00:14:48.660
What the heck...?

00:14:48.660 --> 00:14:50.040
Wow...

00:14:50.040 --> 00:14:51.870
Is this really the place?

00:14:51.870 --> 00:14:54.200
It should be...

00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:55.910
What's all the fuss?

00:14:55.910 --> 00:14:57.790
Don't cause any trouble.

00:14:57.790 --> 00:14:59.120
Sorry about this.

00:15:00.910 --> 00:15:03.200
Sasugai, are you here?

00:15:04.330 --> 00:15:05.580
We're coming in.

00:15:05.580 --> 00:15:07.200
Sasu, you here?

00:15:07.200 --> 00:15:09.040
Sasugai...

00:15:09.040 --> 00:15:10.660
If you're here, then say something.

00:15:10.660 --> 00:15:13.000
Whoa! Wh-What is it?

00:15:13.000 --> 00:15:14.910
What's wrong, Jonouchi?!

00:15:14.910 --> 00:15:17.500
Whoa, stop that! Hey! Ow...

00:15:17.500 --> 00:15:19.450
What is he doing?

00:15:19.450 --> 00:15:20.500
We're going in first.

00:15:20.500 --> 00:15:23.000
Hey, please help me first!

00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:26.290
Ah, sorry, sorry, sorry, sorry, sorry--

00:15:26.290 --> 00:15:27.790
Sasugai?

00:15:31.200 --> 00:15:32.580
This is...

00:15:35.200 --> 00:15:37.200
Wow...

00:15:37.200 --> 00:15:38.370
Excuse me...

00:15:40.870 --> 00:15:42.120
What is this?

00:15:42.120 --> 00:15:44.790
Data for each school, and an
assessment of their abilities...?

00:15:44.790 --> 00:15:47.290
Don't tell me he did this for all the
schools competing in the series?

00:15:47.290 --> 00:15:48.620
Wow...

00:15:48.620 --> 00:15:51.500
He put together all this data by himself?

00:15:51.500 --> 00:15:53.290
This has yesterday's date on it.

00:15:53.290 --> 00:15:54.660
This is from the day before yesterday.

00:15:54.660 --> 00:15:56.540
Wait, this is practice footage?

00:15:56.540 --> 00:15:58.450
How did he film that?

00:16:01.250 --> 00:16:03.870
Aren’t you the challengers?

00:16:03.870 --> 00:16:06.290
"Challengers," huh?

00:16:10.160 --> 00:16:12.160
A plan for a new routine?

00:16:12.450 --> 00:16:14.120
"Takumi Adachi's consecutive
quadruple jumps required!"

00:16:14.660 --> 00:16:15.870
What's that?

00:16:15.870 --> 00:16:19.450
It looks like the schedule
for the ice show the coach goes to.

00:16:31.080 --> 00:16:33.370
The schemer drowns in his own scheme, huh?

00:16:33.370 --> 00:16:35.540
Even Homer sometimes nods.

00:16:35.540 --> 00:16:38.620
At any rate, it was a big gamble.

00:16:38.620 --> 00:16:41.870
In the first competition, your plan wasn't bad.

00:16:41.870 --> 00:16:45.080
"At this rate, it'll be hard to win."

00:16:45.080 --> 00:16:48.290
I'm glad you aren't an idiot.

00:16:51.910 --> 00:16:54.290
Go home. You're interrupting my practice.

00:16:56.250 --> 00:16:58.330
What are you planning?

00:16:58.330 --> 00:17:03.410
Please teach your special move--
that three-quadruple jump combination--

00:17:03.410 --> 00:17:05.830
to Maeshima and the others!

00:17:06.950 --> 00:17:08.910
That Sasugai is...

00:17:08.910 --> 00:17:10.750
...is begging?

00:17:10.750 --> 00:17:13.700
You think that'll make me teach them?

00:17:13.700 --> 00:17:15.750
Why are you going so far?

00:17:15.750 --> 00:17:17.830
Isn't it obvious?

00:17:17.830 --> 00:17:20.250
To win!

00:17:20.250 --> 00:17:24.120
I can't skate. All I can do is leave it to them.

00:17:24.120 --> 00:17:26.580
In order to win, I'll do anything.

00:17:26.580 --> 00:17:31.200
If I can get what I want by bowing
my head, then it's a small price to pay.

00:17:31.200 --> 00:17:34.330
That's the difference between you and me.

00:17:34.330 --> 00:17:36.540
I will never lower my head.

00:17:36.540 --> 00:17:39.000
Not even to ask for instruction.

00:17:39.000 --> 00:17:41.660
You said they didn't trust you, right?

00:17:41.660 --> 00:17:46.040
Then, you should show <i>them</i>
how serious you are, too.

00:17:46.040 --> 00:17:48.700
Skate-leading isn't something
you do by yourself.

00:17:48.700 --> 00:17:52.620
There are five skaters,
and each has their own feelings,

00:17:52.620 --> 00:17:54.700
and their conditions
each day are also different.

00:17:54.700 --> 00:17:59.540
If you can't understand that, then you
aren't good enough as a tactician.

00:17:59.540 --> 00:18:01.250
You're one to talk.

00:18:01.250 --> 00:18:04.080
I'm not about to do anything so annoying.

00:18:04.080 --> 00:18:07.620
Don't reason with them.
Tell them how you really feel.

00:18:07.620 --> 00:18:10.370
Well, it might be too late for that, though.

00:18:14.660 --> 00:18:17.500
It's bad manners to eavesdrop, you know.

00:18:17.500 --> 00:18:20.080
There you go again.

00:18:20.080 --> 00:18:23.330
Bowing your head's a small price to pay, right?

00:18:23.330 --> 00:18:25.200
Damn that guy.

00:18:25.200 --> 00:18:27.330
Oh? Where's Maeshima?

00:18:27.330 --> 00:18:29.290
"Keyaki Park Ice Arena"

00:18:49.450 --> 00:18:53.950
Damn it, it's hard to keep going
after that first quadruple Axel...

00:18:57.120 --> 00:18:59.160
Don't tell me that was...?

00:18:59.160 --> 00:19:03.450
No doubt about it. He was trying
to do the coach's special move...

00:19:03.450 --> 00:19:05.910
He didn't have enough rotations, though.

00:19:11.500 --> 00:19:16.790
Sorry, did I do something
to make everyone mad again?

00:19:16.790 --> 00:19:18.830
I envy you.

00:19:18.830 --> 00:19:19.830
Huh?

00:19:19.830 --> 00:19:23.120
You can move your body however you want,
and you're blessed with talent--

00:19:23.120 --> 00:19:26.120
But how you waste that annoys me.

00:19:26.120 --> 00:19:28.660
But I need you.

00:19:28.660 --> 00:19:31.200
In order to beat that bastard, too.

00:19:31.200 --> 00:19:33.950
So even if you refuse, I'll take you with me.

00:19:33.950 --> 00:19:36.250
That's how I really feel right now.

00:19:36.250 --> 00:19:42.000
Huh? I don't really get it, but I'm here
right now because you said that.

00:19:42.000 --> 00:19:43.500
I'm not gonna quit after all this time.

00:19:43.500 --> 00:19:46.410
And I won't let you quit, either.

00:19:47.580 --> 00:19:50.500
What the heck? Was I the
only one worried about it?

00:19:50.500 --> 00:19:53.450
But weren't you being kinda heartless?

00:19:53.450 --> 00:19:55.790
You weren't worried about Sasugai at all.

00:19:55.790 --> 00:19:57.790
Worried? Why?

00:19:57.790 --> 00:20:00.120
He was absent from school for a long time.

00:20:00.120 --> 00:20:04.540
Huh? It's Sasugai you're talking about.
He was probably just scheming, right?

00:20:04.540 --> 00:20:06.370
There's no reason to worry.

00:20:06.370 --> 00:20:08.580
Is this...?

00:20:08.580 --> 00:20:11.200
Were we just wasting our time...?

00:20:11.200 --> 00:20:15.540
It looks like you were practicing
the three consecutive quads, right?

00:20:15.540 --> 00:20:18.660
Yeah, 'cause you wouldn't teach me.

00:20:18.660 --> 00:20:21.410
That move puts a big strain on your body.

00:20:21.410 --> 00:20:24.000
Stop practicing on your own.

00:20:24.000 --> 00:20:30.910
Unless you plan to sacrifice your
skating career for just one win?

00:20:30.910 --> 00:20:33.000
What are you saying?

00:20:33.000 --> 00:20:37.540
If you don't get the victory right in front
of you, then what is there after that?

00:20:39.290 --> 00:20:42.410
Anyway, stop practicing on your own.

00:20:42.410 --> 00:20:44.410
--But--
--I'll teach you!

00:20:47.870 --> 00:20:51.830
In return, I'll teach it to you properly.

00:20:55.660 --> 00:20:57.700
I see, he refused?

00:20:57.700 --> 00:21:02.250
He said something about not getting
the victory in front of him yet.

00:21:02.250 --> 00:21:05.080
If he thought that, then he should've
refused the coaching position, too.

00:21:05.080 --> 00:21:08.370
That's the shortest way for him, huh?

00:21:08.370 --> 00:21:10.290
Thanks. Later.

00:21:11.500 --> 00:21:14.620
Is that your resolve?

00:21:14.620 --> 00:21:16.910
But it'll be an even harder
path than you imagine.

00:21:16.910 --> 00:21:18.580
"Third Competition Results
St. Clavis Gakuin receives highest scores in history!"

00:21:20.870 --> 00:21:22.500
"Second place in debut match!"

00:21:38.160 --> 00:21:39.200
Are you all right?

00:21:39.200 --> 00:21:41.330
Ouch...

00:21:41.330 --> 00:21:43.750
Oh, I definitely landed that wrong.

00:21:43.750 --> 00:21:45.540
Get it taken care of as soon as possible.

00:21:45.540 --> 00:21:47.580
It's almost time for the next competition.

00:21:47.580 --> 00:21:50.160
If you don't take it seriously,
it could lead to an injury.

00:21:51.540 --> 00:21:54.620
The entry form for the
fourth competition is here.

00:21:54.620 --> 00:22:00.250
In the next match, Shinozaki's team,
St. Clavis Gakuin, will also be skating.

00:22:02.830 --> 00:22:04.870
Is it finally time?

00:23:36.000 --> 00:23:36.950
"Next time" "Champions"

00:23:36.950 --> 00:23:37.790
"Next time" "Champions"

00:23:36.950 --> 00:23:37.790
Terauchi.

00:23:37.790 --> 00:23:38.790
"Next time" "Champions"

00:23:37.790 --> 00:23:38.790
What is it, Himuro?

00:23:38.790 --> 00:23:41.620
"Next time" "Champions"

00:23:38.790 --> 00:23:41.620
Recently, that Tomo's been like,
"Ken and Sasugai did this"

00:23:41.620 --> 00:23:44.290
"Next time" "Champions"

00:23:41.620 --> 00:23:44.290
and "Akimitsu, Jonouchi, Yukimitsu, Kiriyama"...

00:23:44.290 --> 00:23:45.700
"Next time" "Champions"

00:23:44.290 --> 00:23:45.700
All he talks about is you guys.

00:23:45.700 --> 00:23:47.410
"Next time" "Champions"

00:23:45.700 --> 00:23:47.410
Are you a lonely older brother or something?

00:23:47.410 --> 00:23:48.750
"Next time" "Champions"

00:23:47.410 --> 00:23:48.750
--More importantly--
--What is it?

00:23:48.750 --> 00:23:50.950
"Next time" "Champions"

00:23:48.750 --> 00:23:50.950
He doesn't talk about me?
